'''Joshua''' (Japanese: '''ジョシュア''' ''Joshua'') is a supporting character in ''[[Pokémon: Path to the Peak]]''.
==History==
{{incomplete|section}}
In ''[[PTP01|The Club]]'', Joshua witnessed [[Ava]]'s difficulty adjusting to her new school and discreetly placed a Pokémon Club invitation on Ava's food tray. When meeting with Ava, Joshua taught her the basics of the [[Pokémon Trading Card Game]], but because of her inexperience, Joshua managed to win easily.

The next day, he had another match against Ava, being defeated this time. After she managed to defeat all the members of the club, Joshua accepted her into the group. While celebrating, Ava met [[Celestine]], and Joshua soon after explained to Ava who she was and about the upcoming [[Play! Pokémon#Regional Championships|Regional Championships]].

==Character==
Joshua is the leader of the Pokémon Club at the new school that [[Ava]] joined. Joshua also has a catchphrase; ''"Challenge Accepted"'', which he says every time he meets a new person.
==Deck==
Joshua uses a {{e|Lightning}}-based deck focusing on {{TCG ID|EX Delta Species|Jolteon ex|109}}. The deck's strategy uses {{TCG ID|EX Delta Species|Super Scoop Up|100}} to return Jolteon ex to the hand, allowing Joshua to evolve multiple {{TCG ID|EX Delta Species|Eevee|69}} in a single turn for repeated use of Jolteon ex's Evolutionary Thunder {{TCG|Poké-Power}}. {{TCG ID|EX Delta Species|Dragonite δ|3}} is used to accelerate Energy cards using its Delta Charge Poké-Power.

Joshua refers to this deck as his "old deck", and as such, most cards within it are from the EX Series.

